    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁρισ-τής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who marks the boundaries</i> : in pl., <i>officers
				appointed to settle boundaries,</i> public or private, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.94.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Eux.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Heracl.</u>
				1.2
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>TG</u>
				21
			</span></i> ; the chief being called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γαμέτρας</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεωμέτρης</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tab.Heracl.</u>
				1.187
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				9.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				287
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>one who determines,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δικαίων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					15.29
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Stat.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				5.1.5
			</span></i>.</div>
